  "conclusion": "The preregistered single-path hypothesis was rejected. On aligned history, gate-only improved action loss by only 0.02231 percent from base and residual-only regressed by 0.49777 percent, while the full composition improved by 0.48190 percent. The inferred gate-residual interaction was 0.95736 percent of base loss, larger than either marginal contribution. The full path reproduced R5's weak causal sensitivity: aligned beat zero by 0.36145 percent and shuffle by 0.09890 percent, both below the original 1 percent gate. R5 therefore depends on cooperative gate-plus-residual composition while its eight original memory context tokens still remain available; this motivates the dynamic-exclusive R6 probes.",
